    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-10-21T11:21:42+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-21T11:21:42+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-21T00:51:42Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-21T00:51:42Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A trough of low pressure lingers about the east, before weakening later today, as a slow moving high pressure system in the Tasman Sea will re-establish a ridge across southern parts. A trough is then forecast to briefly move into the west on Thursday, before another trough and cold front move more broadly across SA on Friday and Saturday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW013" description="North West Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-10-21T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-22T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-20T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-21T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers north of Coober Pedy, most likely in the evening. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm in the afternoon and evening. Winds northeast to southeasterly 15 to 25 km/h. Daytime maximum temperatures around 30.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">Moderate</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:30am to 5:00pm, UV Index predicted to reach 11 [Extreme]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-10-22T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-23T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-21T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-22T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. High chance of showers north of Coober Pedy, medium chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm, possibly severe with damaging winds and large hail north of Marla in the morning and afternoon. Winds northeast to southeasterly 15 to 20 km/h tending northwest to northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h in the morning then tending northeast to southeasterly 15 to 20 km/h in the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 17 and 21 with daytime temperatures reaching the low 30s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-10-23T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-24T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-22T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-23T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Slight chance of a shower. The chance of a thunderstorm in the afternoon and evening. Winds northeast to southeasterly 15 to 20 km/h tending northwest to southwesterly during the day then tending southeast to southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 16 and 19 with daytime temperatures reaching the low to mid 30s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-10-24T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-25T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-23T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-24T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. High chance of showers south of Coober Pedy, medium chance elsewhere. A thunderstorm likely. Winds south to southeasterly 15 to 25 km/h tending south to southwesterly 25 to 35 km/h during the morning. Overnight temperatures falling to between 14 and 21 with daytime temperatures reaching 22 to 36.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
